1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,547
An image classifier can carry millions of learned weights. But deployment asks a different question. Can

2
00:00:06,547 --> 00:00:11,882
we keep useful intelligence, while using less storage and less time? This is CompressKit.

3
00:00:13,283 --> 00:00:19,732
A convolutional neural network processes an image through layers. Early filters respond to simple patterns, such

4
00:00:19,732 --> 00:00:26,180
as edges. Deeper layers combine these patterns into features. A final classifier produces scores, and the

5
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:28,196
highest score gives the prediction.

6
00:00:29,617 --> 00:00:35,682
We load a trained model and preserve an untouched copy. We export the baseline to ONNX

7
00:00:35,682 --> 00:00:41,748
and measure accuracy, prediction latency, and file size. Training and calibration data stay separate from the

8
00:00:41,748 --> 00:00:43,644
test data used for evaluation.

9
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:50,990
The toolkit checks the CPU for low precision instruction support. Eight bit arithmetic can reduce storage,

10
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:56,929
but speed depends on the hardware and runtime. We use the hardware probe to guide precision,

11
00:00:56,929 --> 00:00:59,157
then verify performance with actual timing.

12
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:07,811
Structured pruning removes entire feature channels. Unlike simply setting weights to zero, this changes the dimensions

13
00:01:07,811 --> 00:01:15,038
of the network. A dependency graph updates connected layers together, preserving compatible shapes, including around residual

14
00:01:15,038 --> 00:01:15,489
connections.

15
00:01:16,917 --> 00:01:24,379
Large cuts can damage accuracy. Gradual pruning alternates smaller cuts with fine tuning. Batch normalization recalibration

16
00:01:24,379 --> 00:01:31,841
updates activation statistics using calibration data. It requires forward passes, without gradient based weight training. Recovery

17
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:36,038
can help, but does not guarantee the original accuracy.

18
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:43,549
The original model teaches the compressed student. The student learns from correct labels and from the

19
00:01:43,549 --> 00:01:49,649
teacher’s output scores. These scores contain relationships between classes. Distillation can recover useful behavior lost during

20
00:01:49,649 --> 00:01:53,842
pruning. The teacher is not needed when the student is deployed.

21
00:01:55,250 --> 00:02:01,601
Quantization represents values using fewer bits. Moving from thirty two bit floats to eight bit integers

22
00:02:01,601 --> 00:02:07,953
reduces raw weight storage by about four times, for the same number of weights. Calibration determines

23
00:02:07,953 --> 00:02:13,510
suitable ranges. Total file reduction varies, and some operations may remain in floating point.

24
00:02:14,917 --> 00:02:22,540
When rounding damages accuracy, quantization aware training simulates reduced precision during training. The weights adapt before

25
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:29,686
final quantization. In our pipeline, the final deployment quantization comes after structural changes and training.

26
00:02:31,117 --> 00:02:37,580
Automatic mode starts with quantization. If only accuracy fails, it can protect sensitive layers, then try

27
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:44,044
quantization aware training and distillation. If size or latency fails, it explores pruning. Each candidate is

28
00:02:44,044 --> 00:02:50,103
measured. The search stops when the requirements are met, if a suitable configuration is found.

29
00:02:51,517 --> 00:02:56,955
In our recorded ResNet fifty six run, model size fell from three point two eight to

30
00:02:56,955 --> 00:03:02,394
zero point five three megabytes. Latency improved by two point two five times. Accuracy changed from

31
00:03:02,394 --> 00:03:07,833
ninety three point one eight to ninety point five zero percent: a loss of two point

32
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:09,192
six eight percentage points.

33
00:03:10,617 --> 00:03:17,253
The final output is an ONNX model, accompanied by an HTML report and machine readable results.

34
00:03:17,253 --> 00:03:23,889
A new image passes through the compressed model to produce a prediction. CompressKit connects established techniques

35
00:03:23,889 --> 00:03:27,208
with hardware awareness, automatic decisions, and honest measurement.